From 51ff6d086b8b98e6d89dffb84ba6449a1f81ac2d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mateusz Bajorski <mbajorski@shasta.cloud>
Date: Wed, 4 Mar 2026 16:01:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pkg/lps: introduce Local Profile Server package
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add a new LinuxKit service package (pkg/lps) implementing the EVE LPS
REST API (PROFILE.md). The server runs as a containerized microservice
on port 8888 and provides:

- GET  /api/v1/local_profile       — advertise a local profile override
- POST /api/v1/radio               — acknowledge radio status, respond with silence config
- POST /api/v1/appinfo             — respond with per-app restart/purge commands
- POST /api/v1/devinfo             — respond with device commands (reboot/shutdown/collect_info)
- POST /api/v1/location            — acknowledge GNSS location reports
- POST /api/v2/edgedevice/.../compound-config — LOC endpoint serving loc-config.bin
- GET  /images/*                   — static HTTP file server for disk images

The server reads config from /config/lps/ (token, profile, radio_silence,
dev_command, app_commands/) and writes state snapshots to /persist/lps/.
Disk images placed in pkg/lps/images/ are bundled via git-lfs, seeded to
/persist/lps/images/ on first boot by lps-init.sh (copy-once, idempotent),
and served over HTTP to EVE's downloader for fully airgapped operation.

zedagent changes:
- Skip AuthContainer signature verification for http:// LOC URLs
  (local-network trust model; no controller signing key in airgap/dev)
- Bootstrap LOC URL from /config/loc/url when no controller-provisioned
  LOC config is available, enabling airgap/dev deployments without
  a cloud controller

Also add /persist/lps/ to storage-init.sh and wire LPS_TAG into
parse-pkgs.sh and images/rootfs.yml.in.

Signed-off-by: Mateusz Bajorski <mbajorski@shasta.cloud>
